---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
const updated = '2026-06-22';
---
<Base
  title="Refund & Cancellation Policy — 24Observe"
  description="How subscriptions, cancellations, refunds, and usage-based charges work at 24observe. Cancel anytime, no lock-in, no surprise charges."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container" style="max-width: 760px;">
      <div class="eyebrow"><span class="bar"></span> Legal · last updated {updated}</div>
      <h1 class="h1">Refund &amp; Cancellation Policy</h1>
      <p class="lede" style="margin-top: 24px;">
        Plain terms for paying, cancelling, and refunds on the 24observe hosted service.
        No lock-in, no cancellation fees, and no charge you can't see coming.
      </p>

      <h2 class="h2" style="margin-top: 56px;">1. Subscriptions &amp; billing</h2>
      <p>
        Paid plans (Team, Business, Scale) are <b>monthly subscriptions</b>, billed in advance on a
        recurring cycle that starts the day you subscribe. Payments are processed by our payment
        provider, <b>Dodo Payments</b>; we do not store your card details. The Free plan is, and always
        will be, $0 — no card required.
      </p>

      <h2 class="h2" style="margin-top: 48px;">2. Usage-based charges</h2>
      <p>
        Log ingestion above your plan's monthly included allowance is billed as metered usage at the
        per-GB rate shown on the <a href="/pricing">pricing page</a>. Usage charges accrue during the
        billing period and are invoiced with your next renewal. Because these reflect resources already
        consumed, <b>usage charges already incurred are non-refundable</b>. Your current allowance and
        any accrued usage are always visible in <i>Settings → Billing</i> before you're billed.
      </p>

      <h2 class="h2" style="margin-top: 48px;">3. Cancelling</h2>
      <p>
        You can cancel any time — there is no minimum term and no cancellation fee. Cancel from the
        dashboard: <i>Settings → Billing → Manage billing → Cancel subscription</i> (this opens our
        provider's secure billing portal). On cancellation:
      </p>
      <ul style="line-height: 1.8;">
        <li>Your paid features remain active <b>through the end of the current billing period</b> you've already paid for.</li>
        <li>At the end of that period the subscription stops renewing and your organization reverts to the Free plan.</li>
        <li>We do not auto-charge you again after you cancel.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="h2" style="margin-top: 48px;">4. Refunds</h2>
      <p>
        Because cancelling lets you keep paid access through the period you've already paid for,
        monthly subscription fees are <b>generally non-refundable</b> for the current period. We will,
        however, promptly refund:
      </p>
      <ul style="line-height: 1.8;">
        <li><b>Duplicate or erroneous charges</b> — billed twice, or charged after a confirmed cancellation.</li>
        <li><b>Verified billing faults on our side</b> — e.g. you were charged for a tier you did not select.</li>
        <li><b>First-time goodwill</b> — if you upgraded and immediately realised it was a mistake, contact us within <b>7 days</b> of the charge and we'll work it out.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Approved refunds go back to the original payment method via Dodo Payments, typically within
        5–10 business days depending on your bank. Downgrading mid-cycle takes effect at your next
        renewal; we don't prorate partial-month downgrades.
      </p>

      <h2 class="h2" style="margin-top: 48px;">5. Failed payments</h2>
      <p>
        If a renewal payment fails, we retry over a short dunning window and email the account owner.
        If it ultimately can't be collected, the subscription is cancelled and the organization reverts
        to the Free plan — your data is not deleted by a payment failure.
      </p>

      <h2 class="h2" style="margin-top: 48px;">6. Deleting your account</h2>
      <p>
        Deleting your organization (<i>Settings</i> → delete) immediately cancels any active
        subscription so you are not billed again, then irreversibly purges your data. See the
        <a href="/legal/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> for data-deletion timelines.
      </p>

      <h2 class="h2" style="margin-top: 48px;">7. Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Billing questions or refund requests: <a href="mailto:support@24observe.com">support@24observe.com</a>.
        Include your organization name and the charge date so we can find it quickly.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
